    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0008:0001",
      "source": "For example, the following code extracts channel `2` from a four-channel pixel buffer.",
      "ko": "For example, the following code extracts channel `2` from a four-channel pixel buffer.",
      "sourceHash": "3b18fae4cb5d3cfffa71178e5910b7006db7d2d86e902246747701e5099d4606",
      "status": "failed"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:code:discussion:0009:0001",
      "source": "```swift\nlet src = vImage.PixelBuffer<vImage.Interleaved16Ux4>(\n    pixelValues: [10, 11, 12, 13,\n                  20, 21, 22, 23,\n                  30, 31, 32, 33],\n    size: vImage.Size(width: 1, height: 3))\n\nlet dest = vImage.PixelBuffer<vImage.Planar16U>(\n    size: src.size)\n\nsrc.extractChannel(at: 2,\n                   destination: dest)\n\n// Prints \"[12, 22, 32]\"\nprint(dest.array)\n```",
      "ko": "```swift\nlet src = vImage.PixelBuffer<vImage.Interleaved16Ux4>(\n    pixelValues: [10, 11, 12, 13,\n                  20, 21, 22, 23,\n                  30, 31, 32, 33],\n    size: vImage.Size(width: 1, height: 3))\n\nlet dest = vImage.PixelBuffer<vImage.Planar16U>(\n    size: src.size)\n\nsrc.extractChannel(at: 2,\n                   destination: dest)\n\n// Prints \"[12, 22, 32]\"\nprint(dest.array)\n```",
      "sourceHash": "88673f46228ca3610ca1d9a6389195ee21425120cfd3dd61b9680e754638c321",
      "status": "preserved"
    },
